A||||3||Eric||N2O setups||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||06-06-2001||12:34 AM||||I'd like to know what kind of nitrous setups fellow forum members have.  I will assume most of you are running on the stock short block and probably heads.  I'm really just trying to figure out an easy approach.<P>Right now I have a an 88 block with the 3.1 crank in it, Federal Mogul hyperetectic pistons (the real limiting factor), gm hipo cam, ported heads, exhaust and all the rest of that performance crap.  The setup is good for low to mid 15s in my 88GT.  What I'm looking for is a little more power to put me solidly into the 14s.  I have some mustang 5.0 injectors that I can clean and use if I have a chip burned.  With those injectors and a adjustable fuel pressure reg. (I already have it), would I need to upgrade the fuel pump?  If so, with what?<P>I realize the problems with hyperetectic pistons and detonation, so I won't go to big on the nitrous jetting.  I was thinking between a 40 and 70 horsepower shot on a dry system.  Anyone have one they want to get rid of? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||06-06-2001||01:50 AM||||I would definitely upgrade the fuel pump.  Best choice would be the Corvette LT4 fuel pump, its good for up to 400 Hp and fits in Fiero's.  I could dig up the part number if you need it.  gmpartsdirect.com sells them for $80.00 shipped.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||06-06-2001||06:50 AM||||Yeah, I was thinking the LT4 pump too.  I wonder with the big pump, adjustable fuel pressure reg., and 19lb injectors, if this thing would just suck gas all the time.  I know 1FST2M6 had giant injectors put on his old SE, but I don't know how that car was on gas or if he had a custom chip burned.  Shaun41178 told me of someone who will make me this chip based on the specs of my engine, but I forgot the web address.  Hopefully these two will be by to comment sometime today.<P>I have an air/fuel meter right now installed in the car.  It just monitors the O2 sensor's readings.  With the engine at WOT, the thing is nearly pegged in the green/rich side (roughly 45# of fuel pressure).  I still get 26 mpg highway.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||06-06-2001||08:24 AM||||why do you want a dry kit? for the same price maybe cheaper you can get a wet kit. I had a fuel pump from an 88 Iroc. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>  <BR>tire lifting torque... this was a dry kit and it was ok.. but the wet kit is WAY better and safer.  MSD 6al,  Accel coil, and huge injectors DUMPING fuel... i got 9-14mpg driving around... and i could use a bit more than 1/8th tank in one 1/4mi run on nitrous. (3 runs 1/2 tank) the stock injectors are ok for a wet kit and a small dry kit. <P>the nitrous info i got for the BEST nitrous kit... tell him Travis from Engineered Performance sent ya. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006347.html</A> <P>Shaun41178 is running a dry kit on his automatic and running 14.0, my best time was 13.6@103. (4spd)... Nitrous ROCKS. neither myself nor Shaun have had a real nitrous related failure. our engines are fine and i'm not sure about shaun but i used mine like it was going out of style... Why have it if your not gunna use it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/travis.jpg</A> <BR>my former nitrous car. <P>let me know if you need more info... <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">      <BR>www.engineered.net<BR>www.epdyno.com<BR>www.enthuzacar.com||||reg||1
